 Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51555"} "Free Pistol, 50 yards, Team, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51536"} "Free Rifle, Three Positions, 300 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51541"} "Free Rifle, Three Positions, 300 metres, Team, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51537"} "Free Rifle, 1,000 yards, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51545"} "Military Rifle, 200/500/600/800/900/1,000 yards, Team, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51552"} "Small-Bore Rifle, 50 and 100 yards, Team, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51534"} "Small-Bore Rifle, Disappearing Target, 25 yards, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51533"} "Small-Bore Rifle, Moving Target, 25 yards, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51538"} "Running Target, Single Shot, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51556"} "Running Target, Single Shot, Team, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51539"} "Running Target, Double Shot, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51540"} "Trap, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "51557"} "Trap, Team, Men"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:span {} "Not held in other editions"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/683"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Small-Bore Rifle, Prone, 50 and 100 yards, Men" [:small {} [:a {:class "footnote", :href "#", :title "There were 62 other entrants who did not compete, from the following nations: Norway (13), Denmark (12), Hungary (10), Sweden (10), France (9), Greece (6), Australia (1), and Germany (1).", :data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right"} "1"]]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "11 July 1908"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/226"} "Bisley Rifle Range, Bisley"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/51535"} "20 from 5 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Prone position. 50 yards and 100 yards. 40 shots at each distance. 200 possible at each distance, 400 total possible."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "In a very controversial event, " [:a {:href "/athletes/42283"} "Arthur Carnell"] " eventually led a British sweep of the first nine places.  But Carnell did not have the highest score in this event.  That honor was left to British shooter " [:a {:href "/athletes/42403"} "Philip Plater"] ", who is not actually considered to have even taken part."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The limit for entrants per nation in all individual shooting events was 12.  But the entry forms for " [:a {:href "/athletes/42263"} "George Barnes"] ", the eventual bronze medalist, were lost, and Plater was named as the 12th British entrant in his place.  However, an extension of the deadline for entries was made, and Barnes’ application was eventually accepted.  On the day of the competition, the British team officials lost count of the number of British shooters who had competed in this event.  With only one-hour to go before the time limit, they called on Plater to shoot, thinking he was the 12th British shooter in the small-bore rifle, when, in fact, he was the 13th - one beyond the limit.  In varying light, a gusty wind, and fine drizzle, he fired his 80 rounds in less than 30 minutes, scoring 391, the leading score and a new world record.  In the initial results issued by the National Rifle Association, and published in " [:em {} "The Sporting Life"] ", Plater was listed as the winner."] "\n\n" [:p {} "But the error of Britain having 13 competitors was then discovered and it took several days to sort out the error.  It was not certain if Plater’s or Barnes’ mark would be deleted from the official results, but eventually Plater was declared an unofficial entrant and not given an Olympic medal.  However, in October 1908, Philip Plater was presented a special gold medal and a record diploma by the British Olympic Council."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th